@flexiarg war-room/wr-19-tension-must-generate-not-only-rank
@title WR-19: Tension Must GENERATE, Not Only Rank
@sigils [⚖/令]
@audience futon stack operators, agents, mission authors
@tone foundational
@style pattern
@why war-room/wr-0-organise-without-apparatus
@holds-at R17
@holds-open R6

! conclusion: Wire structural tension as a candidate source that generates actions, not merely as a weight that ranks candidates generated elsewhere.

  + context: War Room decision WR-19 (2026-05-31). Operator: Joe. A live geometric stack should always give the War Machine something to do.

  + IF:
    The geometric stack detects high-tension regions that should drive the War Machine's next action.

  + HOWEVER:
    The current wiring, ΔT as a sorry-only tie-breaker, cannot generate a move; it only ranks an existing menu, so a system full of unresolved tension still yields nothing when nothing is proposing candidates.
    + EXAMPLE: On its first outing the War Machine exhausted its
      proposer-fed queue into `learn-action-class` before any outward
      open-mission surfaced. Tracing the judge showed why: structural
      pressure was applied only after four fixed proposers had supplied
      candidates, and only to address-sorry candidates. The system was full of unresolved tension and the machine had nothing to do, because a tie-breaker
      cannot put an option on a menu it only reorders.


  + THEN:
    Add a tension-proposer: a component that emits new candidate actions where tension is highest, so the field can put options on the menu rather than only rank the ones already there. Make this the proximate fix to starvation and the first build slice.

  + BECAUSE:
    A ranking signal cannot create an option that is absent from the menu. Tension becomes actionable only when it can propose the candidate whose priority it would otherwise merely increase.

    + evidence: The first outing exhausted its proposer-fed queue into learn-action-class before any outward open-mission surfaced; tracing futon2.report.war-machine/judge found structural pressure applied only after four fixed proposers had supplied candidates, and only to address-sorry candidates.
